{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793188063,"nonce":"Bx2gvApJgqky9MI0+oHttNXtk4I=","title":"Keep RayScript previews closed until opened in an Ashui Sheet","message":"Opening a .rays source currently creates an inline preview column inside its editor group. With existing splits this unnecessarily reduces source and preview width. Keep source editors full-width, add a Preview toolbar control, and open the preview in Ashui's existing right-side Sheet. Preserve group layout, close the sheet on tab changes, and avoid starting a source preview before it is requested. Use Sheet lifecycle, close/Escape handling and styling rather than a custom drawer implementation.\n\nValidate default-hidden/lazy startup, existing split dimensions, all Pocket Studio module previews and their controls, and close/reopen cleanup in native and browser targets.","files":null}]}